From b81333bd5bb0ec481fd5b6fcc114a0bd800dce71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 05:31:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Tiled sparse attention: tile metadata on the GPU, no host
 sync

build_tiles used Python loops over cu_seqlens/prefix_lens lists, and the wrapper read them
with .tolist() on every layer; each read synchronized the stream, serializing kernel launch
with execution 60 times per prefill chunk. The tile count is now bounded from shapes
(total_q // tile + num_reqs), the tile -> request map is a GPU searchsorted, and surplus
tiles carry zero rows and exit at once. Outputs unchanged (tests/gpu/test_sparse_attn_tiled.py).
